<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to June 7.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to June 7.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to June 7 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week June 1-June 7</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97	 605,118 tns	 62,434 tns    10.32 pct</p>
<p>     95-96	 262,800 tns	 26,952 tns    10.26 pct</p>
<p>     94-95	 667,016 tns	 68,346 tns    10.25 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to June 7</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    41,232,609 tns    4,450,128 tns    10.79 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    39,859,546 tns    4,348,930 tns    10.91 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    39,573,407 tns    4,219,121 tns    10.66 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 30 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 16 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 27 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
